{
  "about": "What a driver must receive for each kind of typed input: the tables of docs/argument_casting_ground_truth.md as data, one entry per row (ids match the doc). Run against example/edge_case_sdl.py (EdgeCaseSDL: every method takes one argument called `value` and keeps what it received) by tests/automated/test_casting_ground_truth.py here and by the legacy repo's copy of this file. Inputs: `typed` is the text a person typed (a string, or a list of strings that must all give the same result); `json` is a value that reaches the edge already typed (an optimizer suggestion, an older frontend, a legacy workflow); `omitted: true` also runs the case with the argument left out of the call. `expect` is `{value: <Python repr of what the driver got>}` or `{refused: <substring of the message, matched ignoring case>}`. `surface`: `field` (a single value: the Designer step, Instruments, the Once form), `cell` (a spreadsheet cell; the walk is client-side, so the Python test skips these), `both`, `run` (needs a queued run, not only a call), `schema` (an expectation on the published schema), `import` (a legacy workflow converted by the Designer's import, the launcher and classic.py; not a cast). `status` is the doc's: agreed, or a difference the legacy copy marks as known. The Python version a run was checked on is recorded by the test run, not here.",
  "instrument": "edge_cases",
  "markers": { "none": "<None>", "default": "<default>" },
  "cases": [
    { "id": "P1", "status": "agreed", "case": "int given 2.5", "method": "take_int", "annotation": "int", "typed": "2.5", "surface": "both", "expect": { "refused": "whole number" } },
    { "id": "P1.ok", "status": "agreed", "case": "int given 3", "method": "take_int", "annotation": "int", "typed": "3", "surface": "both", "expect": { "value": "3" } },
